# Maintain compact single-viewport Studio and accessible dialogs

- Match Blossom's established professional dark audio UI and requested mockups; do not invent a separate generic AI design system.
- Main Studio and Connections desktop workspaces fit vertically without page-level scrolling; allow bounded inner regions/dialogs where necessary so no critical controls are hidden.
- Support mobile/narrow viewport, keyboard focus, labelled inputs, reduced-motion, clear error/loading/empty states and accessible modal close/Escape.
- Actions must visibly update after one click and prevent accidental duplicate submissions; preserve the current project selection and unsaved edits.
- Clearly label local AI vs OpenAI API, manual provider browser login vs verified authorization, Music DNA evidence and background job progress.
- Verify rendered geometry and interaction with viewport and Playwright tests; do not use Playwright to automate Google's login flow.
